  "body": "## What changed\n\nA tool library file (`.camtools`) now keeps the drawn cutter (`ToolCutter`) of a tool. Before this change, export and import dropped it.\n\n- `crates/app/src/tool_library.rs`:\n  - `export_tool_library` writes the drawn cutter as `cutter`. These are the `[z, r, arc]` points that a `.camproj` tool stores.\n  - A file with one or more cutters says version 5 (`CUTTER_VERSION`). A file without a cutter keeps version 4 or lower.\n  - `parse_tool_library` reads `cutter` and judges it with `cutter_profile::check`. This is the same check as the project loader (`cutter_from_dto`). A cutter that disagrees with its tool, or a malformed cutter, refuses the whole file by tool name.\n  - `LibraryTool` has a new field `cutter`.\n- `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import/mod.rs`: `ImportTools` sets the cutter on Add, Update and Replace. Undo restores the previous cutter in the same undo step. A library tool without a cutter keeps the cutter of the document on Update (the same law as the body). A tool that is the same in all but its cutter is now an update, not a skip.\n- No `.camproj` change: the project file carries `cutter` since #93 slice 2.\n- `crates/app/src/tool_table.rs`: the new field (`cutter: None`).\n- `crates/app/tests/holder_reference.rs`: the \"future version\" of an existing test is now `CUTTER_VERSION + 1`.\n- `docs/decisions/3904-camtools-cutter.md`: the decision.\n\n## What an older build does\n\nA build that reads version 1 to 4 refuses a version-5 file: `tool library version 5 is not supported (this build reads 1 to 4)`. It does not drop the cutter silently. Since #852 the stack laws read the neck of a drawn cutter, thus a dropped cutter gives a different tool. This follows the `HOLDER_REF_VERSION` precedent (#2016).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `crates/app/tests/tool_library.rs` (the existing suite, now 19 tests):\n\n- `a_drawn_cutter_round_trips_through_the_library_file`\n- `a_cutter_that_disagrees_refuses_the_file_by_tool_name`\n- `update_replaces_the_cutter_in_one_undo_step`\n- `a_library_without_a_cutter_keeps_version_4_or_lower`\n\n## Gate (Windows, `winbuild`)\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head `4592f2e2b`, trial-merged with `origin/main` (`83e5e8a37`), `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`:\n\n- 18 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 4.5 min.\n- app build, app lib (307), `cutting_unknown_row` (9), `holder_reference` (7), `mcp` (48), `plasma_cut_data` (3), `scripting` (20), `tap_hand` (7), `tool_body_assembly` (5), `tool_catalog_fields` (7), `tool_cutting_rows` (11), `tool_import_modes` (9), `tool_library` (19), `tool_library_holders` (8), `tool_reservations` (6), `tool_reservations_extra` (7), `tool_table` (6), `waterjet_machine` (13).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nEarlier runs:\n- The first head re-exported two functions from `app::project`. That selected 191 steps, and the app build stalled while it linked 180 test binaries (the watchdog killed it at 15 min). The head now calls `cutter_profile::check` directly, and the plan is 18 steps.\n- One run was red on two tests. `holder_reference` used `HOLDER_REF_VERSION + 1` as a future version, which is now valid. A malformed `cutter` is refused earlier by the definition reader, with a different message. Both tests are fixed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No heavy lane (this is not a `P1` change, and no post or toolpath changed).\n- No GUI check. This PR has no UI change, thus no screenshots.\n- MCP `export_tool_library` and `import_tool_library` call the same functions. Their schema does not change. No MCP test was added for the cutter.\n\nChangelog: Tool library files (.camtools) keep a tool's drawn cutter outline. A file with one says version 5, and an older build refuses it.\n\nEffort: high (file format).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nFixes #3904\n",
